[18,1,5,'5.0',`The diagram shows triangle <i>ABC</i>. <i>ABD</i> is a straight line.${PD({w:159.4,h:122.8,g:[["n|k|1","M129.4 16L105.1 106.8L14 106.8L121.7 44.7"],["n|k|0.5","M47.3 106.8C47.3 100.7 45.6 95.1 42.8 90.2M112.5 79.2C110.1 78.6 107.6 78.2 105.1 78.2C89.3 78.2 76.5 91 76.5 106.8M126.1 28.3C124.7 27.9 123.2 27.7 121.7 27.7C112.3 27.7 104.7 35.3 104.7 44.7C104.7 47.7 105.6 50.6 107 53.1"]],t:[[80.4,100.5,13,"100°"],[35.2,103.6,13,"x"],[113.2,42.6,13,"y"],[131.1,19.2,13,"D"],[123.3,50.8,13,"B"],[106.7,114.8,13,"A"],[0.6,111.4,13,"C"]]},'Triangle ABC with angle 100° at A, angle x at C and exterior angle y at B')}<p class="tiny">NOT TO SCALE</p>Angle <i>x</i> is acute and angle <i>y</i> is obtuse. Find <b>one</b> possible pair of values for angle <i>x</i> and angle <i>y</i>.`,`Any pair with 0 &lt; <i>x</i> &lt; 80 and <i>y</i> = <i>x</i> + 100, for example <i>x</i> = 30°, <i>y</i> = 130°`],
[19,2,13,'',`The diagram shows shape A and shape B.${PG([-8,8],[-6,6],[['poly',[[4,1],[0,4],[0,0],[4,0]]],['txt',[2.2,1.4],'A'],['poly',[[-3,-4],[-6,0],[-2,0],[-2,-4]],'rgba(120,120,120,.2)'],['txt',[-3.3,-1.7],'B']],{u:20,label:'Shape A with vertices (4, 1), (0, 4), (0, 0), (4, 0); shape B with vertices (–3, –4), (–6, 0), (–2, 0), (–2, –4)'})}Shape A is transformed onto shape B by a combination of <b>two</b> transformations. The first is a rotation of 90° clockwise about (0, 0). Describe fully the <b>second</b> transformation.`,`Reflection in the line <i>x</i> = –1. 1 mark for reflection and 1 mark for <i>x</i> = –1`],
[20,2,1,'1.3',`Put each calculation in the correct region: ‘Less than 8<sup>6</sup>’, ‘Greater than 8<sup>6</sup>’, ‘Equal to 1’, or outside all of them. A is done for you (Less than 8<sup>6</sup>).<p class="m">A: 8<sup>2</sup> × 8<sup>2</sup> &nbsp; B: 8<sup>2</sup> × 8<sup>3</sup> &nbsp; C: 8<sup>15</sup> ÷ 8<sup>5</sup> &nbsp; D: 8<sup>0</sup> &nbsp; E: 8 × 8<sup>5</sup> × 8 &nbsp; F: (8<sup>2</sup>)<sup>3</sup></p>`,`B: less than 8<sup>6</sup>. C and E: greater than 8<sup>6</sup>. D: equal to 1. F (= 8<sup>6</sup>): outside the circles. 1 mark for three or four correct`],
[21,1,8,'',`True or false?<br>(1) Fractions with an even denominator will <b>always</b> be equivalent to a terminating decimal.<br>(2) Fractions with a denominator which is a multiple of 9 will <b>always</b> be equivalent to a recurring decimal.`,`(1) false, (2) false (both for the mark)`],
[22,3,12,'',subs([['a','Naomi has a bag of 5 counters, each with a different number, and a bag of 10 counters, each with a different letter. She picks one counter at random from each bag. One outcome is 3F. Find the total number of possible outcomes. [1]'],['b','Naomi has 5 white cards numbered 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 3 grey cards numbered 2, 3, 4. She picks one white card and one grey card at random. Calculate the probability that both cards show a number greater than 3 [2]']]),subs([['a','50'],['b',F(2,15)+'. 1 mark for '+F(2,5)+' × '+F(1,3)+', or a correct sample space of 15 outcomes with 2 marked']])],
[23,3,3,'3.1',`It is given that 0.71 × 10<sup><i>n</i></sup> = 71 and 2.3 × 10<sup><i>p</i></sup> = 0.000 23. Find the value of 0.067 ÷ 10<sup><i>n</i> + <i>p</i></sup>`,`6.7. 1 mark for <i>n</i> = 2 and 1 mark for <i>p</i> = –4`],
[24,3,2,'2.4',`Here is an algebraic statement. <p class="m">(<i>x</i> + 3)<sup>2</sup> + <i>c</i> = (<i>x</i> – 3)(<i>x</i> + 5) + 4<i>x</i></p>Find the value of <i>c</i>.`,`<i>c</i> = –24. 2 marks for both expansions correct (<i>x</i><sup>2</sup> + 6<i>x</i> + 9 and <i>x</i><sup>2</sup> + 2<i>x</i> – 15); 1 mark for three correct terms in one expansion`]
